+  <div class="side">
+    <h1>AquaAlert - the 30-second version</h1>
+    <p>Small farms lose a season's income in one bad night. Big companies see it coming through
+    probes and lab tests; a 1-hectare farm cannot. This screen shows the verdict, <b>why</b>,
+    and the one action that matters - at 05:30, in the farmer's own language.</p>
+
+    <h2>How it works without sensors</h2>
+    <ul>
+      <li><b>Free weather API = the oxygen sensor.</b> Hot, still, rainless nights drive pre-dawn
+      dissolved-oxygen crashes. Open-Meteo gives us that for free, globally, no key.</li>
+      <li><b>₹15 ammonia strip + pH + thermometer = the ammonia photometer.</b> We convert total
+      ammonia into toxic NH<sub>3</sub> with the FAO/Emerson pH-temperature model.</li>
+      <li><b>Public pond datasets = the baselines.</b> IoT pond datasets give the normal diurnal
+      shape; the pond's own history gives the drift alarm.</li>
+      <li><b>Public fish photos = the vet.</b> 2,444 CC0 South-Asia images + 1,043 annotated
+      tilapia images train the photo triage.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>Alert escalation</h2>
+    <table class="t">
+      <tr><th>Band</th><th>Channel &amp; timing</th></tr>
+      <tr><td style="color:#6ddc9c">GREEN</td><td>App only (and silence - never spend an SMS on good news)</td></tr>
+      <tr><td style="color:#ffd54f">YELLOW</td><td>SMS, once per 6 h, + cooperative dashboard</td></tr>
+      <tr><td style="color:#ff9e5e">ORANGE</td><td>SMS + Kannada IVR call + photo request</td></tr>
+      <tr><td style="color:#ff8a80">RED</td><td>SMS + IVR + extension officer paged, re-check every 6 h</td></tr>
+    </table>
+
+    <h2>Cost per farm</h2>
+    <div>
+      <span class="tag">Verdict ~₹0</span>
+      <span class="tag">SMS ~₹0.15</span>
+      <span class="tag">IVR ~₹0.60</span>
+      <span class="tag">ammonia strip ~₹15/test</span>
+      <span class="tag">hardware optional</span>
+    </div>
+    <p style="font-size:12.5px;color:#9dc9ae">Optional upgrade path: ₹700 ESP32 + DS18B20 + pH
+    module feeds the same API - the system is designed so hardware can be added later without
+    changing the farmer's screen.</p>
+
+    <div class="foot">Sources: FAO x6709e ch.2.5 &amp; AC175E18 ch.18 (ammonia chemistry) &middot;
+    eXtension/SRAC water-quality table &middot; El-Sherif &amp; El-Feky 2008 via PMC9640449 &middot;
